<title>UK: UK Home Office says it will scrap 1,200 jobs.</title>
<headline>UK Home Office says it will scrap 1,200 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Home Office said on Friday that it would lay off 1,200 people because it was introducing a new computer system to speed up processing of immigration cases.</p>
<p>About 800 jobs will be scrapped in the ministry's Immigration and Nationality Department in 1998-99 and a further 400 the following year. The losses amount to around 20 percent of the department's current staff.</p>
<p>Officials said they expected that around 750 people will be made redundant. The remainder of the jobs will be lost through retirement and not filling vacancies.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
